CHAPTER.VERS:
But after they had 

          He declares how God's mercies always contended with the wickedness of the people, who always in their prosperity forgot God.
         rest, they did evil again before thee: therefore leftest thou them in the hand of their enemies, so that they had the dominion over them: yet when they returned, and cried unto thee, thou heardest [them] from heaven; and many times didst thou deliver them according to thy mercies;
